What are CSS and SCSS?

CSS — controls how your webpage looks: colors, spacing, font sizes, borders, layouts, and more.

SCSS — an enhanced syntax for CSS that supports features such as variables and nesting. It gets compiled into regular CSS for the browser.

The line styleUrl: './app.css' tells Angular which CSS file to use for this component.

h1 {
  color: darkred;
  text-align: center;
}

h1 — the selector; it targets all <h1> elements in this component's template.

{ } — contains the styling rules.

color — changes the text color.

darkred — the value assigned to that property.

text-align: center — centers the heading horizontally.


